        "committer": {
          "name": "Di Wang",
          "email": "diwa@nvidia.com",
          "date": "2026-11-12 03:47:22.000000000",
          "tz": -480
        },
        "subject": "LU-21194 tests: use PAGE_SIZE in sanity 150f, 151 and 156",
        "message": "LU-21194 tests: use PAGE_SIZE in sanity 150f, 151 and 156\n\nsanity 151 and 156 (via roc_hit_init) write the file with bs=4k and\nexpect the OSS cache_access/cache_hit counters to rise by one per 4k\npage.  With 64KiB pages, 4k writes fill a single page, so a 16KiB read\nraises the counter by 1 instead of 4 and the tests fail with \"roc_hit\nis not safe to use\".  Write whole PAGE_SIZE blocks so that the number\nof pages written, and so the expected counter change, is the same for\nany page size.\n\nsanity 150f expects a 20KiB file to use 40 sectors and 24 after\npunching 8KiB.  The OSD maps and writes whole pages, so with 64KiB\npages the last page is fully allocated: the file uses 128 sectors, 112\nafter the punch, and the test fails with \"punch failed: blocks 112 !=\n24\".  Add the unused part of the last page to the expected counts.\nAlso keep the second sub-case (a 3000 byte punch, which frees no whole\nblock) at the full allocation.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nChange-Id: I3f3fbd6cd967f5962d58d7bc7644fe020f1f05d7\nSigned-off-by: Di Wang <diwa@nvidia.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-sonnet-5-5 ltvm\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
